cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated research article and dataset."
type: software
title: "PANDA v2.10 Surface-Finishing Workspace Assessment: Reproducibility Code"
version: "0.1.0-rc1"
authors:
  - given-names: Aleksandar
    family-names: Simov
    affiliation: "Institute of Robotics, Bulgarian Academy of Sciences, Sofia, Bulgaria"
    email: a.simov@ir.bas.bg
  - given-names: Tanio
    family-names: Tanev
    affiliation: "Institute of Robotics, Bulgarian Academy of Sciences; Center of Competence Smart Mechatronic, Eco- and Energy-Saving Systems and Technologies, Sofia, Bulgaria"
    email: tanevtk@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  MATLAB postprocessing and numerical verification scripts
  supporting configuration-consistent kinematic and inertial
  workspace assessment for robotic surface finishing.
  The package reproduces screening, paired inertial loading,
  pose-matched contrasts, and threshold sensitivity from
  archived configuration-level numerical data.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - robot manipulability
  - inertial workspace assessment
  - surface finishing
  - reproducibility
  - MATLAB
